From 53c8685517ca77347d7abe2f646cfa21bdb62895 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:49:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Kanban wake: a queued wake is relabelled from live
 card state when the drain claims it

PR #1305 relabelled a stale premise (chat_wait_unclaimed, blocked, crashed, ...) only when a later
wake folded into the queued row. A row nothing folded into ran with the text it was built with:
MacBook row 3605 (2026-11-12) would have told its chat that t_01a1ce7ed2addb09, claimed ~15 min
earlier, had no worker.

execute_admission now rebuilds a claimed kanban-wake row's text from its stored kanban_cards with
the fold's own refresh_card/compose path, just before the turn is built, beside the stale block-ask
refresh (same in-memory payload, never the stored row). Every card keeps its
"[kanban] Task <id> <kind>." line. An unreadable board, another producer's row, or text that no
longer has the shape its cards built leaves the text unchanged.

Task: t_01a1cfc175c64298
